Z||000002||theogre||10-10-2000||09:38 AM||||Can't say much for USB on a PC. Haven't had any problem with the IMacs. USB KB and mice are all you can get for them.<P>Sounds like either the PC's USB has a problem of the KB is bad. You could have a resource problem on the system board. Even tho PCI devices are suposed to be able to share interupts it doesn't always work. (The PC I'm using right now crashes if I allow PCI interupt shares.)<P>The other thing you could try is delete the USB resources in system properties and let WinWhatever redetect it on the next bootup. (You'll want a regular KB and mouse hooked up to do this.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||10-10-2000||09:47 PM||||I just decide it was too much fun pounding this POS into a wad of plastic on the floor. My flash card reader and other USB stuff works fine (even when plugged into the usb ports on the keyboard!) so I carefully placed the little device on the floor and jumped up and down on it until I got tired. Hmmmmm, maybe I should back off on the coffee.||||reg||1
